<title>USA: U.S. June personal income rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. June personal income rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department personal  income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates,  including annual revisions released Friday.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Jun    May--(Prev)   Apr--(Prev)   Mar</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.6    0.3    0.3    0.2    0.2    0.6</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.5    0.3    0.3    0.1    0.2    0.5</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.4    0.3    0.3   Unch    0.1    0.4</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.3    0.3    0.3    0.1    0.1   Unch</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.1    0.3    0.4   Unch   Unch   Unch</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Jun    May--(Prev)   Apr--(Prev)   Mar</p>
<p> Income		   6,866  6,824  6,774  6,800  6,754  6,788</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,874  5,842  5,836  5,828  5,821  5,821</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,616  5,601  5,539  5,584  5,522  5,580</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,445  5,430  5,368  5,414  5,352  5,411</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   643    646    645    643    644    654</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,582  1,578  1,583  1,577  1,585  1,589</p>
<p> -Services		3,220  3,206  3,139  3,194  3,123  3,168</p>
<p> Personal Savings	 259    242    298    244    298    242</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 4.4    4.1    5.1    4.2    5.1    4.2</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Jun    May--(Prev)   Apr--(Prev)   Mar</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,867  3,835  3,838  3,822  3,828  3,821</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   702    700    700    700    700    698</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,378  1,354  1,357  1,348  1,353  1,348</p>
<p> -Government		663    662    658    661    658    660</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    546    543    554    541    553    537</p>
<p> -Farm			 45     45     46     44     46     41</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  501    499    508    497    507    496</p>
<p>--ANNUAL REVISIONS TO PREVIOUSLY RELEASED DATA--</p>
<p>Percent changes with previously reported figures in parenthesis.</p>
<p>				 1996	    1995	   1994</p>
<p>Income (current dollars) 5.6 (5.5)     6.2 (6.1)    4.9 (4.8)</p>
<p>--Chained dollars:</p>
<p>Disposable Income	  2.3 (2.9)     3.3 (3.3)    2.2 (2.2</p>
<p>Consumption		  2.6 (2.5)     2.4 (2.3)    2.3 (3.1)</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected personal income for June to rise 0.4  percent and spending to increase 0.4 percent.</p>
